title The room becomes construction
prompt Keaton approved the expanded prompt and then set a top standfast ahead of it -- breach-rename crux/ to construction/, as more Gauge-friendly and closer to what the Comlink tendency asks of a name.
think Measured before moving: 109 tracked files, 1,442 path occurrences across 620 files, split 144 living and 476 dated testimony. Checked construction was free -- no tracked path, nothing in the Lexicon.
think The load-bearing distinction is that crux is a seated Lexicon term for the hardest solvable problem, with 4,162 living uses. So the sweep had to move the PATH form and leave the WORD entirely alone -- replace crux/ with a slash, never bare crux.
think A breach rather than a debride, so nothing is rewritten and the walk-back stays reachable everywhere. Cairn recorded and committed before the move.
think Applied both lessons the previous rename of this same room paid for. REDS %153: no compatibility symlink -- and I went further and removed the dangling work-in-progress one it left behind. REDS %155: sweep the machinery in the same pass as the prose, rather than a lap later.
obs Five guards reddened, and every one was honest. banner_room found two archive banners still claiming the crux shelf. documented_room found ORGANIZING.md naming work-in-progress as a room, which had only ever passed because that untracked symlink resolved. foundations_link found four broken why-room links, three of them to work-in-progress, stale since the ELDER rename and hidden by the same symlink.
obs So removing the symlink surfaced two pre-existing faults that had been invisible for eight days. That is the same finding as REDS %153 arriving from the other side: an untracked compatibility link does not only blind a guard, it hides the work the guard exists to demand.
obs The last two reds were mine, and the lesson has now fired four times. My blanket repoint rewrote paths INSIDE two control pens -- tools/fixtures/phantom_path_control.sh and tracked_link_control.sh plant their own crux/ directory and symlink to it, and the sweep renamed the writes while leaving the mkdir and the ln -s pointing at a room the pen no longer built. A control is instrument, never field, and a sweep across the tree meets one.
obs Fixed by making each pen internally consistent rather than by excluding it -- the pen now builds construction/ and links to construction/, so it mirrors the tree it measures.
loom breach files_moved=109 occurrences=1442 files_touched=620 living_repointed=491 living_files=144 testimony_untouched=476 guards_red=5 guards_fixed=5
file construction/ the room, renamed from crux/ with 109 files carried
file construction/CAIRNS.md the walk-back recorded before the move
file ORGANIZING.md the workbench entry repointed, naming both elder names it carried
file tools/fixtures/phantom_path_control.sh the pen builds and links the room it writes to
file tools/fixtures/tracked_link_control.sh the same repair
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the breach is landed and all twenty-seven guards are green. Four more renames are now queued behind it: Skate to Surf with Surf Social, cairn to checkpoint, manual/glow-os to grain-os, and your name back to Keaton Dunsford, that last one a deep debride across every commit. Each is a separate breach wanting its own cairn, and I would rather take them one at a time than braid four renames into one sweep -- this round showed a single rename touching 620 files and reddening five guards.
